<title>USA: Texaco, Shell to merge some U.S. businesses.</title>
<headline>Texaco, Shell to merge some U.S. businesses.</headline>
<dateline>WHITE PLAINS, N.Y. 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Texaco Inc said on Tuesday that it and Shell Oil Co have agreed to combine the major elements of their United States refining and marketing activities in the Midwest and West, as well as their total U.S. transportation, trading and lubricants businesses.</p>
<p>The new company, to be 56 percent owned by Shell and 44 percent owned by Texaco, will market gasoline under both company's brand names through independent wholesalers and retailers.</p>
</text>
